-- ============================================================
-- Warrior (Protection): Toughness scales block value off Strength
-- ============================================================
-- TODO.md: "Toughness (0, 0): (As today plus) doubles block value scaling from
--           Strength. (5 ranks)"
--
-- "(As today plus)" is literal: Effect1 (armour +2/4/6/8/10%) and Effect2
-- (movement slow duration -6/12/18/24/30%) are untouched.  Effect3 was free.
--
-- Toughness also MOVES to Tier 0 Col 0 in this batch -- see
-- woa_2026_08_09_07.sql for the swap with Improved Bloodrage and the
-- prerequisite-arrow check.
--
-- Ranks ramp to the doubling rather than granting it at rank 1: the effect
-- carries 10/20/30/40/50 (percent of the Strength contribution to add), so 5/5
-- adds a second full Strength * 0.5 and the scaling is exactly doubled.  Rank 1
-- being a taste rather than a spike matches how the armour ranks already
-- behave.
--
-- Base points are 9/19/29/39/49 with DieSides 1, because
-- CalcValue = BasePoints + max(1, DieSides).  The description prints the result
-- with $s3, so the tooltip reads 10..50 with no help from the script.
--
-- Why this needs C++ at all, in one line: Player::GetShieldBlockValue
-- (Player.cpp:5115) hard-codes Strength * 0.5f and nothing in Spell.dbc scales
-- block value off a stat.  spell_warr_toughness_blockvalue
-- (modules/world_of_alonecraft/src/WarriorToughness.cpp) computes the amount of
-- this effect and heartbeats it every 2 seconds so it follows gear; the effect
-- slot, the aura type, the percentages and the prose are all here.  The header
-- of that file explains why the flat term is the correct place to land.
--
-- Spells:
--   12299 / 12761 / 12762 / 12763 / 12764 = Toughness ranks 1-5
-- ============================================================

